From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Clint Goudie-Nice <clint-goudie-nice@example.net>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:34:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] igmp_fsm: read each reported source once, not one past the
 list

mcgrp_update_group_address_table() refreshes the remote flag of each
source of a report with `for (i = 0; i <= src_cnt; i++)`: the `<=` gives
the no-source case its one pass, and with sources it reads src_array
[src_cnt], one source past the list -- 4 bytes for IGMPv3, 16 for MLDv2,
past the end of the packet when the record is the last one. Every
well-formed report whose last record lists sources does it.

Loop once when there are no sources and once per source otherwise.
---
 src/igmp_fsm.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/igmp_fsm.c b/src/igmp_fsm.c
index 7115bbb..6d149a9 100644
--- a/src/igmp_fsm.c
+++ b/src/igmp_fsm.c
@@ -2012,7 +2012,9 @@ MCGRP_MBRSHP *mcgrp_update_group_address_table(MCGRP_CLASS *mcgrp,
 
         if (!mbrshp_del)
         {
-            for (i = 0; i <= src_cnt; i++)
+            /* once with no sources (the (*,G) entry), else once per source:
+             * i <= src_cnt read one source past the report's list */
+            for (i = 0; i < (src_cnt ? src_cnt : 1); i++)
             {
                 /* 
                  * If the type of (S,G) /(*,G) entry is changed between remote to dynamic or viceversa, 
